e people are reporting from Hisham, which they are claiming that Hisham might have a problem. So you have 18 people reporting from Hisham, great scholars of hadith. If this narration had an issue, they would all criticize, they would all weaken this narration. So the reason scholars like Bukhari and Muslim included this narration is because you have all of these routes in all of these different cities. It's mass reported from him.", "But it's not only from Hisham, like I said, remove Hisham from the the equation. You still have al-Aswad al-Qasim ibn Abdur Rahman, you have Amrah bint bint Abdur Rahman, Yahya ibn Abdur Rahman. Qasim ibn Abdur Rahman, I'll I'll go on and on and on. So there is so many others that narrate this narration and and they narrate it directly without going through Hisham ibn Urwah. But does it does it even stop there? Because he says like we don't look at other ahadith narrated. So you have another hadith in in Imam Ahmad, it's not even from Aisha herself.", "Some people say that oh maybe Aisha she which is like kind of criticism or that she didn't know her age. You have other people reporting which not not Aisha, they're not reporting from Aisha they're other people reporting the narration. They're reporting the incident. We have this narration in Musnad of Imam Ahmad. So we have Abu Salamah and I don't know if you guys know who Abu Salamah is. He's one of the seven fuqaha of Medina if if you guys know who were the fuqaha of Medina, great scholars of Medina. He's one of these seven fuqaha of Medina.", "You also have Yahya ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn Hatib also in this narration in Musnad Ahmad. You have two people here. Two authentic, reliable people, great people or from the greatest tabi'in reporting. And they don't report from Aisha in this narration. They They don't say they heard Aisha. They report the incident. They report an incident where it mentions the age of Aisha and it's in in Musnad Ahmad. So, is it really that it is one narration, one